# M6: Android release-signing credentials. COPY this file to
# `android/key.properties` and fill in your real values. The real key.properties
# and the keystore (*.jks / *.keystore) are git-ignored — NEVER commit them.
#
# For Google Play this is the UPLOAD key: Play App Signing (enrolled in the
# Play Console at first upload) holds the real app-signing key at Google.
# The upload key only authenticates your uploads — but back it up anyway:
# losing it means a reset flow through Play support.
#
# 1. Generate a keystore (once), keeping it OUTSIDE the repo:
#      keytool -genkeypair -v -keystore ~/pitak-upload.jks -keyalg RSA \
#              -keysize 2048 -validity 10000 -alias pitak-upload
#    (keytool prompts for passwords + your name; or use -storepass:env /
#     -keypass:env to avoid passwords in shell history)
# 2. Copy this file:  cp android/key.properties.example android/key.properties
# 3. Fill the four values below. NOTE: modern keytool creates a PKCS12 store,
#    which requires keyPassword == storePassword (a different keyPassword is
#    silently ignored at creation and then fails signing with "Given final
#    block not properly padded").
# 4. Back up the keystore + passwords securely (password manager / encrypted
#    backup). The same keystore also signs local release APKs.

storeFile=/absolute/path/to/pitak-upload.jks
storePassword=CHANGE_ME
keyAlias=pitak-upload
keyPassword=CHANGE_ME
